<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Not a PDF</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>This is HTML, not a PDF.</h1>
    <p>
      The extension says .pdf and the browser will declare it as
      application/pdf, so every check short of reading the bytes waves it
      through. The first five bytes are "&lt;!doc", not "%PDF-", which is what
      the server's magic-byte check actually decides on.
    </p>
    <script>
      document.title = "if this ever executes, something served it as HTML"
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
